   "about" : "End-to-end Image::PHash 0.3 golden for a fixed 32x32 synthetic RGBA image (channels: r=(i*1103515245+12345) mod 2^32 low byte, g=(i*1664525+1013904223) mod 2^32 low byte, b=(i*22695477+1) mod 2^32 low byte, i in row-major scan order). The Go NewFromImage pipeline resizes the 32x32 fixture to 32x32 (ApproxBiLinear identity), extracts luminance (r*0.3 + g*0.59 + b*0.11), DCTs it, and runs the bit pipeline; the Perl reference here computes Math::DCT dct2d over the same luminance with a fake Image::PHash instance (im_scaled set, no cached dct) and empty/zero pHash options, so the scalar-context return value (b2h of the bit string) is the golden hex for NewFromImage with default settings.",
